=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play environment ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Environment screen proposed for slice 9,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (sudoers.Choose, Read, PlanFor), each change on the real$
# plan/apply engine (steps.Sudoers). Who ran hardn, the reader$
# of hardn's files and the plan's findings on the change are the$
# gallery's, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Environment hosts ############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13            sudo, not kept$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04         sudo-rs, not kept$
   3) Alpine 3.23          doas through wheel$
   4) Alpine, refused      doas: treatment doas-refuse$
   5) Alpine cloud image   wheel.conf read after$
   6) doas, overridden     hardn's rule, wheel.conf after$
   7) Proxmox VE 9         no sudo$
   8) Kept                 hardn-env-alice there$
   9) Kept, toggle         Treatment item1-toggle$
  10) Root login           Not run with sudo$
  11) hardn's grant        hardn-grant-alice there$
  12) Grant, no reader     An env-only Policy$
  13) Legacy file          /etc/sudoers.d/alice$
  14) Legacy, unread       Treatment legacy-hardn-only$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-14 or q]: 6$
$
# Info: environment/doas-overridden$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23's cloud image, doas; alice$
# is in wheel, and cloud-init's /etc/doas.d/wheel.conf says$
# permit nopass :wheel (the maintainer's VM). alice ran doas$
# hardn. hardn's rule for alice keeps HARDN_CONFIG, but$
# wheel.conf's wins, so doas dropped it.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under doas           Kept$
   -  /etc/doas.d/wheel.conf may override it$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under doas           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# Environment hosts ############################################$
$
  Select a host$
$
   1) Debian 13            sudo, not kept$
   2) Ubuntu 26.04         sudo-rs, not kept$
   3) Alpine 3.23          doas through wheel$
   4) Alpine, refused      doas: treatment doas-refuse$
   5) Alpine cloud image   wheel.conf read after$
   6) doas, overridden     hardn's rule, wheel.conf after$
   7) Proxmox VE 9         no sudo$
   8) Kept                 hardn-env-alice there$
   9) Kept, toggle         Treatment item1-toggle$
  10) Root login           Not run with sudo$
  11) hardn's grant        hardn-grant-alice there$
  12) Grant, no reader     An env-only Policy$
  13) Legacy file          /etc/sudoers.d/alice$
  14) Legacy, unread       Treatment legacy-hardn-only$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-14 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

